1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,650
Now a year has more
than 1,000 days in it.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,790
Meanwhile,
the calendar breaks.

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,190
But every day
gets shorter,

4
00:00:08,195 --> 00:00:10,670
so a year contains
more days.

5
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,505
Right now,
at a 6 hour day,

6
00:00:13,505 --> 00:00:18,250
a year already holds
about 1,460 days.

7
00:00:18,587 --> 00:00:21,497
By the end,
it would hold over 6,000,

8
00:00:21,782 --> 00:00:25,562
with a sunrise every
84 minutes, and you

9
00:00:25,562 --> 00:00:28,667
would be asked to sleep
eight times a day.

10
00:00:28,705 --> 00:00:32,100
At the poles, the ground
only turns on the spot.

11
00:00:32,418 --> 00:00:35,338
Nobody there is carried
around at all,

12
00:00:35,338 --> 00:00:37,768
and they would weigh
the same as ever.

13
00:00:37,915 --> 00:00:40,365
At 45 degrees north,

14
00:00:40,365 --> 00:00:43,970
you move at 70 percent
of the equator's speed,

15
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:47,465
and the push outward
is only half as strong.

16
00:00:47,653 --> 00:00:50,313
The farther you stand
from the equator,

17
00:00:50,473 --> 00:00:52,593
the longer you
keep your weight.

18
00:00:53,058 --> 00:00:54,823
Quick break:
like and follow.

19
00:00:55,063 --> 00:00:57,378
Then let's see
how bad this gets.

20
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:00,370
But the water leaves
the poles first,

21
00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:02,480
so the stillest
place on Earth

22
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,445
would stand high and dry.

23
00:01:04,713 --> 00:01:06,833
And the days keep
getting shorter.

24
00:01:07,085 --> 00:01:08,985
Part six of eight.
